WEBVTT

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.100
Dad! Dad!

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:08.440
Welcome, Sei.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.040
Today is your celebration.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.740
Yeah!

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.680
Come on in.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.530
Congratulations on making the
best 16 in the World Tournament!

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:35.430
And welcome back from traveling
around the world to promote Gunpla.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.570
Sei, I brought you a present.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.610
Thanks, dad!

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.520
How wonderful it is to love Gunpla!

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.690
Hurray for Gunpla!

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.970
It was a dream.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.900
I wonder where dad is right now?

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.930
Hello, everyone!

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.860
I'm the image character of the
Gunpla Championship World Tournament,

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:54.100
Kirara, the Gunpla idol!

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.100
<i>﻿Kiraran!</i>

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.900
<i>﻿It's day 10 of the World Tournament.</i>

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:01.910
<i>﻿The qualifier periods are over,</i>

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:06.840
<i>﻿and 16 teams have been selected
to advance to the tournament finals.</i>

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:09.980
<i>﻿Before the finals
that will start in 3 days,</i>

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.780
<i>﻿we have here with us...</i>

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:16.120
<i>﻿Rainer Cziommer of Germany, who was
unfortunately eliminated in the qualifiers!</i>

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:20.320
<i>﻿Mr. Cziommer, what can we
expect to see next?</i>

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:26.660
Who could've guessed
Sei and Reiji would still be in.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.070
<i>﻿I'm gonna make it nice and clear.</i>

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.770
<i>﻿Fellini will lose.</i>

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.040
<i>﻿He'll be totally crushed.</i>

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:40.340
<i>﻿You must have really bad taste
if you're into a loser like that.</i>

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:43.280
<i>﻿Mr. Cziommer!</i>

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.950
I'm all dressed and ready!

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:50.050
Now I can deal with those reporters.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:58.030
Could you tell us
how you raised Sei Iori?

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.100
I didn't do anything special.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:04.000
I just hoped he'd become
a kind and honest boy.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.710
Your husband Takeshi was runner-up
in the 2nd World Tournament.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:10.310
Now your son Sei is in the best 16.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.010
Yours is truly a Gunpla family.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:14.380
And you're so beautiful, madam!

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.080
Oh, stop.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.950
Doors locked!

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:25.860
Wait for me, Sei and Reiji.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:29.790
Mom's coming to cheer for you!

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:43.770
My bad, Sei.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.810
I'm sorry I broke it.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:49.250
You don't have to keep saying that.
It couldn't be helped.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.980
I mean, our opponent was
Mr. Fellini after all.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:58.090
But will you be able to fix it for
the tournament finals in two days?

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:02.130
It's okay.
Kousaka and Mr. Ral are going to help.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:05.730
Hey! I'll help too!

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:11.100
No you won't.
You've never built Gunpla before.

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:14.410
It's a piece of cake for me.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:16.970
Here, let me see.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:19.610
- What!?
- ﻿Let go.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:21.050
No!

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:24.050
I said no!

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:36.260
How could you!?

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:38.630
It's because you wouldn't let go.

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:41.630
Don't bother me anymore.

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:43.300
I'll work alone!

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:47.340
Okay, okay I got it.

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:51.240
You're so bossy just because
you're good at Gunpla building.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.040
Where're you going, Reiji?

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:56.650
None of your business!
You told me not to bother you.

00:05:56.650 --> 00:05:58.150
Bye.

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:04.320
That's what happened.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:06.160
Don't fight.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:08.360
No, we're not fighting.

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:14.500
This could be a good
development for Reiji.

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:20.270
At least he's interested
in Gunpla building now.

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:36.690
Y-Yummy!

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:41.030
How come Japanese food is so delicious?

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:45.160
This may just be a local specialty,
but it's still so good.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:48.430
Hurray for "Exotic Japan”!

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.800
Mommy. Mommy.

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:55.840
Buy me a Haro!

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:57.610
Fine, fine.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:10.350
I wish I could stay
in this country forever.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:25.400
Just you wait, Sei.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:29.310
I'll build an amazing Gunpla
so you can't brag anymore.

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:31.340
But...

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:35.250
L﻿ooking at these again,
there sure are a lot of them.

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:39.420
Just how many different kinds
are there of these Zaku things?

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:45.520
Lalah Sune's Mobile Armor?

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.060
Is this a Gunpla's name?

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:50.530
There's a whole story behind it.

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:55.600
It looks like this is
your first time buying Gunpla.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.630
Who are you, old man?

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:02.470
I'm just a passing Gunpla fan
traveling around the world.

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:07.040
If you're having trouble,
I can choose a Gunpla for you.

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:09.310
Huh? Who asked you to...

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:11.820
Let me see.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:12.980
He's not listening.

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:19.790
Oh, this is good.

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:22.490
It's the Beginning Gundam

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:26.460
the main machine in Model Suit
Gunpla Builders Beginning G.

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:30.700
This machine was the first one
that its controller Haru Irei built.

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:33.340
It's distinguished by
its range of movement.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:37.110
It has high mobility in Gunpla Battle
even when assembled normally.

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:42.050
- It has a beam rifle and 9 beam sabers...
- ﻿Don't get carried away, old man!

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:44.620
Who's that guy?

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:48.020
As for the young lady
peeking from over there...

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:49.250
Huh?

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:51.290
For you,

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:55.460
- ﻿I'd recommend the Command Gundam.
- Me?

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:56.290
You're...

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:00.960
I-I've never built Gunpla before.

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:04.640
Then I'll teach you!

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:07.400
See, I have all the tools.

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:14.210
What're you doing here?

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:16.550
It's just a coincidence.

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:18.920
Anyway, who is that old man?

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:20.020
How would I know?

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:22.320
Stop your whispering!

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:25.260
Eliminate distraction
from your Gunpla building!

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:28.830
You're like a totally different person.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.660
You're supposed to say "Sir, yes sir"!

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:33.060
Otherwise, keep quiet!

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:35.170
- Sir, yes sir!

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:40.570
First, open the Gunpla box
and take out the instructions.

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:44.540
Read the instructions carefully.

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:46.580
You have one minute!

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:47.380
Impossible!

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:50.480
Sir, yes sir!

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:54.520
Before you start, check the parts.

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:58.860
Make sure everything shown
in the instructions is in the box.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:02.060
Don't forget the polycaps and stickers!

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:06.700
Start building from
step one in the instructions.

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:11.900
Pay close attention
when using the nippers!

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:17.210
Cut the gate slightly long,
and then trim the extra bit.

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:19.540
﻿It's more effective
to make two cuts.

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:25.680
Assemble the parts you cut out
as per the instructions.

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:28.690
Be careful not to forget the polycaps.

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:32.560
Removing the sticker will
weaken its adhesive strength.

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:35.430
Position it carefully!

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:40.360
It's more effective to
rub it on with a cotton swab.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:46.740
Check the machine's
movement range as you build.

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:51.380
A deep understanding of your Gunpla
will be an advantage in battle.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:56.710
- Finished, sir!
- ﻿Finished, sir!

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:00.220
Wonderful.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.350
I can't believe it's your first time.

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:04.860
They're built diligently
according to the basics.

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:07.620
You both did a good job.

00:11:08.260 --> 00:11:11.630
To commemorate your
first time building Gunpla,

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:14.100
keep the nippers and sandpaper.

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:16.500
- He's back to normal.
- He's back to normal.

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:21.310
We may as well
give the Gunpla a little extra touch.

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:25.040
Panel-lining with a marker
and adding some matte spray...

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:27.810
They'll be transformed!

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:30.110
- Sir, yes sir!

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:32.980
Well, I'm off.

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:35.550
Please be careful, Chairman.

00:11:35.550 --> 00:11:39.420
Miss Baker, while I'm away, take care of...

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:44.660
Yes. I'll think of a new plan
before the tournament finals.

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:46.100
Please do.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:55.970
Chairman Mashita's off on business.

00:11:55.970 --> 00:12:00.840
Now, how am I going to
I'll get into the PPSE factory?

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:05.080
It'd be quicker if
I got close to Meijin Kawaguchi,

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:08.320
but they'll catch me if I'm careless.

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:10.790
What did you say!?

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:15.030
Wait a minute.
The assignment is over.

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:19.200
Your pride won't allow it?
I don't care.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:22.370
The assignment is pointless
if it's outside the tournament!

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:23.800
What's going on?

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:25.300
That's enough!

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:28.010
Don't let it go public!

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:29.870
Hello? Hello?

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:41.650
- Sir! Panel-lining with marker is done!
- ﻿Sir! Panel-lining with marker is done!

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:43.920
Good. On to the finish!

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:45.560
- Sir, yes sir!

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:52.060
When it comes to Gunpla,
he suddenly changes.

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:54.900
He reminds me of someone.

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:02.970
How's it going, Iori?

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:06.640
Can you fix the Gunpla by
the tournament finals in two days?

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:09.650
Just about, yeah.

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:12.250
Don't worry!

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:14.990
I'll cheer you on until you finish it.

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:17.550
You'll stay here until I'm done?

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:20.560
Um...

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:29.830
Even if it gets late,
I'll be sure to take her home.

00:13:30.770 --> 00:13:33.440
Th-Thank you very much!

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:47.980
W-Wow!

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:51.620
Just with those little touches
the old man taught us,

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:54.620
I can't believe they
look so much better.

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:58.730
Gunpla gets better and better
the more you add to it.

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:03.200
Coloring, a change of weapons,
customizing the machine...

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:05.970
It's as unlimited as your creativity.

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:09.370
That's the fun of Gunpla,
and also its profundity.

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:13.080
Great, let's try them out!

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.150
Can you battle?

00:14:15.150 --> 00:14:17.010
- Huh?
- Gunpla Battle!

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:21.020
I've never done anything like that.

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:23.020
I don't even know how.

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:25.490
Alright, whatever.

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:28.430
I can't help it.

00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:30.130
It's alright.

00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:35.700
The battle system here has an unmanned
machine so you can play against the computer.

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:39.740
You can enjoy a battle on your own.

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:46.110
<i>﻿Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:14:52.650 --> 00:14:55.990
<i>﻿Field 1, Space.</i>

00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:59.290
<i>﻿Battle start.</i>

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:04.730
Reiji, Beginning Gundam, let's go!

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:16.410
How great is the Gunpla I built?

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:20.780
Okay, okay. It's good.

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:24.480
Even if it's your first time
controlling the machine,

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:26.580
if you built it yourself,
it's easier to master it.

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:28.220
Exactly.

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:32.490
Let's see who my opponent is...

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:36.430
I've seen that machine before.

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:41.160
It's huge.

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:43.930
That Gunpla was made by
putting claws on a Zeong.

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:49.440
How did such a well-customized Gunpla
get into the battle system?

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:56.080
What!?

00:15:58.750 --> 00:15:59.980
The arms came off!

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:01.620
That's an all-range attack!

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:07.490
Darn!

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:10.730
There's no opening

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:12.860
Reiji!

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:14.500
Darn you.

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:17.030
I worked so hard
to build this Gunpla...!

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:19.770
Th-This is...

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:24.170
This is how Sei must've felt
during every battle.

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:28.580
And unlike mine, his Build Strike...

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:32.780
takes days or weeks to build.

00:16:32.780 --> 00:16:33.650
Ahead!

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:42.230
Charge right up to him!

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:50.100
Amuro Ray, the Gundam pilot,
defeated Char's Zeong that way!

00:16:58.610 --> 00:17:01.380
Oh no! I forgot it had legs.

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:02.850
What a liar!

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:12.420
Backup?

00:17:14.190 --> 00:17:16.530
I can't watch this any longer!

00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:17.990
<i>﻿You!</i>

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:19.000
Here come the arms!

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:40.520
Without the arms...

00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:42.220
All that's left is...!

00:17:42.550 --> 00:17:45.520
- That humongous...
- ﻿Body!

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:18.420
<i>﻿Battle ended.</i>

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:21.830
Yeah!

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:22.990
We did it.

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:24.830
You're good.

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:27.260
Of course. Who did you think I am?

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.940
I thought you'd never
played Gunpla Battle before.

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:38.070
I-I learned by watching you operate it.

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:40.140
It was surprisingly easy.

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:41.080
Seriously?

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:43.450
Of course.

00:18:44.150 --> 00:18:46.780
Anyway, how long are you
going to hold my hand!

00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:48.490
You held mine first!

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:50.820
- No, I didn't!
- ﻿Yeah, you did!

00:18:54.490 --> 00:18:56.190
- ﻿Wait a minute.
- What?

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:58.460
Where's the old man?

00:18:58.460 --> 00:19:00.000
Huh?

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.500
Where did he...?

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:08.710
I knew as soon as I saw
that customized Zeong.

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:11.670
I didn't think I'd meet you here.

00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:17.680
Sometimes he's the owner of
a back-alley model store.

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:20.480
And sometimes he's a Gunpla fan,

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:23.990
traveling around the world
to promote Gunpla.

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:25.620
But his true self is...

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:32.860
International Gunpla Battle
Official Referee, Takeshi Iori!

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:35.770
Gunpla mafioso "C".

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:39.440
I'm arresting you for 36 crimes, including...

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:42.810
illicit participation in an official tournament
and unlawful Gunpla control!

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:59.420
Don't use Gunpla for foolish things.

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:04.030
What!?

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:07.560
You built this
Beginning Gundam yourself!?

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:12.800
What do you think?
Building Gunpla is a piece of cake.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:17.210
He didn't just assemble it.

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:21.410
He drew in the panel lines
and even used matte spray.

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:23.110
So cool.

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:26.620
You really made this by yourself?

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:31.720
Well, I did have a little help.

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:32.960
Who helped you?

00:20:33.190 --> 00:20:35.990
An old man who was usually calm,

00:20:35.990 --> 00:20:38.900
but got real strict
when we built Gunpla.

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:41.730
Oh yeah, he gave me this!

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:45.700
Th-Those nippers...!

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:46.370
What is it?

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:50.640
Oh. It's nothing.

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:56.010
Dad...

00:20:59.280 --> 00:21:00.650
Sorry, Sei.

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:04.650
I'll still be roaming
the world in disguise, but...

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:06.560
I've been watching you on TV.

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:08.930
You've become a good builder.

00:21:08.930 --> 00:21:10.730
Good luck in the tournament finals.

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:13.660
Sei...

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.870
I'll do my best, dad.

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:27.740
With the Build Strike I made...
And together with Reiji.

00:23:02.940 --> 00:23:04.640
Sei! Reiji!

00:23:04.910 --> 00:23:07.540
Congrats on making the tournament finals!

00:23:07.540 --> 00:23:09.680
I came to cheer for you!

00:23:09.680 --> 00:23:11.180
Thank you, Sei's mom.

00:23:11.380 --> 00:23:13.980
Mom, what about the store?

00:23:13.980 --> 00:23:16.190
I closed it for a while.

00:23:16.190 --> 00:23:18.090
But what about the store's sales?

00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:19.690
Don't worry.

00:23:19.690 --> 00:23:20.960
B-But...

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:23.090
Let it go. She's here now.

00:23:23.090 --> 00:23:25.400
Well, I know but...

00:23:26.360 --> 00:23:27.630
Oh, mom!

00:23:28.400 --> 00:23:29.300
Yes?

00:23:30.600 --> 00:23:33.070
Well... Dad was...

00:23:34.610 --> 00:23:38.440
I'm finally back in Tokyo
and here to see you, but...

00:23:39.810 --> 00:23:41.440
Why is it closed?

00:23:41.510 --> 00:23:44.450
It isn't a holiday, is it!?
Why is the store closed!

00:23:44.450 --> 00:23:46.920
Are you mad because
I've been gone so long?

00:23:46.920 --> 00:23:49.090
Open the store, Rinny!

00:23:49.090 --> 00:23:50.490
Rinny!

00:23:50.920 --> 00:23:54.920
Rinny, I love you!

00:23:55.890 --> 00:23:58.290
It's time to settle things
with Mr. Sei and Mr. Reiji.

00:23:58.290 --> 00:24:01.500
I'll show you the mysteries
of my Gunpla Shingyo school.

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:03.200
Next episode, "Model of the Heart".

00:24:03.200 --> 00:24:05.060
Ready, go!
